{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To the wilderness, etc.</b> That is, and if you ask: from where did they know the place of his encampment in the great wilderness? — therefore it says <b>where he was encamped there</b>, etc., meaning, Moses had already informed him of the place where Elohim had spoken with him there, for He had said to him (Exodus 3:12) ״תַּעַבְדוּן אֶת הָאֱלֹהִים עַל הָהָר הַזֶּה״, and He made known to him the mountain upon which they would receive the Torah. And this is the meaning of his saying ״where he was encamped there, at the mountain,״ etc. — known to him. And you will find that they of blessed memory said (Exodus Rabbah, chapter 4) that Moses told Jethro about the matter of receiving the Torah, and I have written this at the beginning of the parashah, so that the making known of the mountain of Elohim is included in what he informed him."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:25.632343061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}